{"case_id":"C042","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["boundary-state gap","input-semantics gap","semantic-oracle gap"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__swizzle_ycc__general__triangle_filter","wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__swizzle_ycc__general__box_filter","fuzz_swizzle_ycck"],"reason":"H0 invokes the changed YCC paths, but materially under-tests their pixel traversal and write semantics. It limits width to 1–63, so the triangle filter's 672-pixel chunk transition is unreachable; it fills every source plane with a single repeated byte, masking spatial indexing, upsampling, and stride errors; and it never validates destination pixels, so incorrect results from wuffs_base__pixel_buffer__set_color_u32_at can pass silently.","evidence":["fuzz_swizzle_ycck computes width as `(63 & (hash >> 8)) + 1`, while wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__swizzle_ycc__general__triangle_filter advances chunks with `end = x + 672u`.","The three source planes are initialized with `memset(src0.ptr, s0, src0.len)`, `memset(src1.ptr, s1, src1.len)`, and `memset(src2.ptr, s2, src2.len)`, making each plane spatially uniform.","Both changed functions write each output through `wuffs_base__pixel_buffer__set_color_u32_at(dst, x, y, color)`.","After wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__swizzle_ycck returns, fuzz_swizzle_ycck checks only `status.repr`; it does not inspect or compare `dst_pixbuf` contents."],"recommended_action":"Extend fuzz_swizzle_ycck to generate widths around 671–673 and larger multiples, populate planes with non-uniform per-row and per-column data, and compare dst_pixbuf against an independent scalar/reference conversion across both triangle and box filtering and the existing destination pixel formats."}
